  "provenance": {
    "class": "mixed: lookup + executed + retrieved + rule-based",
    "lookup": "the 56 survivors and the enumerated structures are rows in the ML-HTVS release; this framework did not recompute them",
    "executed": "log10 ionic conductivity produced by running ML-SSE model.joblib @ e1b7665ebc578e41f3974d276c11887ead6221cb362209e9eb3676e85235de0f; not measured, and not a published score for these 56 formulae",
    "retrieved": "literature cards come from a real query against the authors' corpus; every citation is checked against the project .bib and unverifiable keys are dropped and counted",
    "virtual_feedback": "the Experiment Feedback interface runs at simulation grade: published AIMD trajectories from LiSSE-MP (10.1021/acs.jpcc.3c02908) are served for exact-stoichiometry and same-system matches. Conductivities come from deserializing the authors' own DiffusionAnalyzer objects (pymatgen environment recorded per row), which recomputes their MSD statistics from their stored displacements. This run used no measurement, and the three linked releases contain no measured-cell result used here",
    "rule_based": "next-step suggestions are fixed rules fired by executed flags, retrieved counts, and the published virtual feedback; no composition is proposed and no threshold is invented",
    "threshold_origin": "no accept/reject gate at any stage; 1e-4 S/cm is a field convention used as an annotation only",
    "determinism": "coordination, execution, the fixed rules, and the AIMD lookup over pinned bytes are deterministic given the recorded pymatgen environment. Retrieval is not bit-exact: the embedding service returns scores that move in the third decimal, so a paper within about 0.01 of the floor can enter or leave the retained set between runs (one such flip observed across three runs). Card prose is model-generated and varies freely. Full-chain tests assert structure and inequalities and do not lock prose; one regression test locks a formula substring of the committed snapshot's card verdict",
    "limitations": "composition-level model blind to crystal structure; out-of-training elements flagged; retrieval reports corpus content, not ground truth; no cell was measured",
    "evidence_scope": "multi-agent tool composition on real data, not a validated discovery",
    "does_not_change": "ml_htvs_screening and ml_htvs_continuation are untouched"
  }
